{"schema":"LAW_EN_DOCUMENT_V1","id":"i18n-8347281dc2109afedded4b99cfbe723d5da07a512ee76109","family_id":"KR:012159","country":"KR","language":"en","title":"Special Act on Investigating the Truth of the April 16 Sewol Ferry Disaster and Building a Safe Society","title_original":"4ㆍ16세월호참사 진상규명 및 안전사회 건설 등을 위한 특별법","kind":"법률","source_version":"284117","promulgated":null,"effective":null,"translation_status":"AI_DRAFT","body_status":"BODY_LOADED","source_url":"https://www.law.go.kr/LSW/lsInfoP.do?lsiSeq=284117","source_sha256":"c141291f23520264444e31f7c7002ae169ff7b5f49b50f81aade863d8c364da6","body_sha256":"faa52d08aee04cab07ee3951f69298b8a1f1ab82d1a7f5477d37bb166b261a08","article_count":1,"full_text":"Article 9 (Commissioners' Independence in Performing Duties and Guarantee of Status) (1) No Commissioner shall be subject to outside instruction or interference in performing his/her duties.\n  (2) No Commissioner shall be dismissed from office against his/her will, except in any of the following cases:\n  1. If a Commissioner finds it substantially difficult to perform his/her duties due to a physical or mental disability;  \n  2. If a sentence of imprisonment without prison labor or severer punishment imposed on a Commissioner becomes final and conclusive.  \n  (3) Where a Commissioner falls under paragraph (2) 1, the Inquest may require him/her to retire by a resolution passed with the concurrent vote of at least two-thirds of all incumbent Commissioners.\n","metadata":{"author_method":"Exact held-source units translated or completed using explicitly recorded source/target spans; original official records remain unchanged. All new units are MACHINE_TRANSLATION and UNREVIEWED.","author_title_record":{"path":"D:\\lawsofkorea\\projece\\07_법률번역\\06_법령별다국어완성\\LAW12_20261018_1442\\workc_1129_2094\\review_pending\\WORKC_G01_P04\\1525_KR012159\\translations\\act\\en.title.json","sha256":"4c74ab84248a6134281cf6996ae8261b572ae5b9e5754e6ad1e8c39880d0d84f"},"author_unit_artifact